The mischief pass is done and the worker and extension suites pass. The e2e suite couldn't run here, and the new popup and copy have never been seen in a real browser. I did not commit or push, and I did not touch `.dev.vars` or `.env`.

**User-visible changes**
- **Copy:** every user-facing string now lives in `extension/lib/strings.js`. Errors say what happened and what to do next, for example "The spirits can't reach your Worker (…). Check the URL in Settings and try again." Success reads "Remembered N page(s). It'll haunt you later." Empty states read "Nothing haunts this list yet…".
- **Ghost guide:** the popup has a small inline-SVG ghost that bobs, plus one hint line that names the next step. When nothing is configured it says "Boo. Start by connecting your Worker. Tap "Set up my ghost" below." Once configured, the hint follows this priority: sync error, paused, just synced, pages waiting, page can't be remembered, all quiet.
- **Accessibility:** the ghost is `aria-hidden` and the hint is real text in a polite live region. It holds still under `prefers-reduced-motion`.
- **Polish:** focus rings are now visible on every control. `--faint` text is darker, so it meets AA contrast. Buttons have a minimum height. Show and Copy buttons have `aria-label`s, and the read-only config boxes are named. Inline styles moved into the CSS files. Clipboard failures now show a message instead of failing silently.
- **Not changed:** the manifest, storage keys, Worker API and security model.
- **Test-relied strings:** the e2e script now accepts "Sync hiccup" as well as "Sync problem". The other strings the tests match (`Last sync:`, `Connected`, `Won't remember`) are unchanged.

**Files changed**
- **Extension:**
  - New: `extension/lib/strings.js`.
  - Edited: `background.js`, `popup.html`, `popup.js`, `options.html`, `options.js`, `options.css`, `onboarding.html`, `onboarding.js`, `ui.css`.
- **Tests:** new `extension/test/strings.test.mjs`; edited `tests/e2e/run.mjs`.
- **Docs and spec:**
  - New: `.kiro/specs/ghost-mischief/` (`requirements.md`, `design.md`, `tasks.md`).
  - Edited: `README.md` (credits row, spec link, test count, logs list) and `docs/kiro-logs/README.md` (s15 entry).
- **Release zips:** the three zips under `release/`.

**Tests**
- Worker vitest passed 53 of 53.
- Extension tests passed 43 of 43, including 3 new ones that check every error contains an instruction and that the stable strings didn't drift. I had to run `npm ci` in `extension/` first, because jsdom wasn't installed.
- **e2e did not run.** Chromium fails to start because `libatk-1.0.so.0` is missing. I tried `npm run test:e2e` once; it crashed at launch, and I restored `shots/e2e-results.json`, which it had overwritten. Because the browser was unavailable, I took no new screenshots. The README says the popup screenshots predate the guide, and task 16 in the spec covers the e2e run and the screenshots. As a stand-in, I ran `popup.js` in jsdom for three states (not configured, queued pages, error on a non-capturable page). The hint, last-sync and site lines came out as expected.

**Zips**
- Rebuilt: yes. The manifest stays at 1.0.0.
- `build-chrome.mjs` produced `release/ghost-from-the-past-chromium-v1.0.0.zip`, and `build-firefox.mjs` produced `release/ghost-from-the-past-firefox-v1.0.0.zip`. Each has 35 files.
- No script writes the `-extension-` zip, so `release/ghost-from-the-past-extension-v1.0.0.zip` is a byte copy of the Chromium zip. Both had the same layout before.
- All three zips contain `lib/strings.js`, and the extension zip's `popup.html` has the ghost guide.

I did not do a Meta Llama copy review; the README credits row says so.
